Purpose: On macOS a top level window is opaque, so the sidebar material (vibrancy) behind a document is covered. A root attribute macostranslucent makes the window transparent so the material shows. Upstreamable: small, behind an attribute that nothing sets in Firefox.
Test: ./mach test swell/tests/app/browser/browser_spaces.js --headless

diff --git a/dom/xul/ChromeObserver.cpp b/dom/xul/ChromeObserver.cpp
